      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for the breakdown. The debris/contamination and piston issues sound plausible. Actually, we've also noticed some strange, almost localized pitting on the rotor surface that doesn't seem to align with any of the standard wear patterns we've modeled. It’s like something is small and localized, causing these tiny, sudden disruptions. Does that kind of pinpointed, irregular surface damage suggest anything specific regarding the thermal breakdown?",
